# What a release tarball leaves out. The repository keeps the working notes
# -- the reviews, the wiring notes, the release retrospectives and the agent
# definitions -- because the reasoning in them is the useful part and the
# roadmap links to them. A release is the program, its documentation and its
# assets, and nothing that was only ever for the people building it.
.claude/            export-ignore
.github/            export-ignore
.gitattributes      export-ignore
docs/marketing.md   export-ignore
docs/rc-assessment.md export-ignore
docs/release-0.1.0.md export-ignore
docs/review.md      export-ignore
docs/wiring-notes.md export-ignore
